{"node":{"id":"HP:0003200","label":"Ragged-red muscle fibers","ic":5.273,"definition":"An abnormal appearance of muscle fibers observed on muscle biopsy. Ragged red fibers can be visualized with Gomori trichrome staining as irregular and intensely red subsarcolemmal zones, whereas the normal myofibrils are green. The margins of affect fibers appear red and ragged. The ragged-red is due to the accumulation of abnormal mitochondria below the plasma membrane of the muscle fiber, leading to the appearance of a red rim and speckled sarcoplasm."},"diseases":[{"id":"MONDO:0013971","label":"leukoencephalopathy-thalamus and brainstem anomalies-high lactate syndrome","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_37744cc2ff60","source":"MONDO:0013971","target":"HP:0003200","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:614924 · OMIM:614924","url":"https://omim.org/entry/614924","level":"curated","date":"2012-11-20","confidence":0.5,"snippet":"Combined oxidative phosphorylation deficiency 12: Ragged-red muscle fibers [TAS]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.5,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"curated"},"confidence":0.5},{"id":"MONDO:0009783","label":"progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions, autosomal recessive 1","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_c9da7b1b6881","source":"MONDO:0009783","target":"HP:0003200","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:258450 · PMID:34777884;PMID:32042919","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34777884;PMID:32042919/","level":"observed","date":"2022-05-30","confidence":1.0,"snippet":"Progressive external ophthalmoplegia with mitochondrial DNA deletions,autosomal recessive: Ragged-red muscle fibers (frequency 2/2) [PCS]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":1.0,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"observed"},"confidence":1.0},{"id":"MONDO:0011835","label":"sensory ataxic neuropathy, dysarthria, and ophthalmoparesis","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_a60fb9bc836e","